Astrophysics (@astrophysics: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_1JY0RVDDS0SYCX3BXSQNX5EXE7
Astrophysics explains celestial systems through physical laws and observations. The material covers stars, stellar evolution, galaxies, compact objects, interstellar matter, and high-energy phenomena, connecting nuclear, gravitational, electromagnetic, and statistical physics with astronomical measurements and computational models.

**Common preparation developed:** the [stellar balance lesson](../../core/Build-a-bounded-stellar-model-from-gravity-pressure-and-energy.lingua) introduces shell mass and hydrostatic balance, energy accounts and bounded pressure models, connected onward to populations, interstellar matter and galactic mass evidence. Detailed stellar evolution, compact objects, transport and high-energy research remain pending.

**Parent:** [Universe and space](../Universe-and-space.lingua#r_38KB376VFZ30BXTGB9K0HG55ZP).
} r_1JY0RVDDS0SYCX3BXSQNX5EXE7
